 Crustates installer  0.2.0  amd64  UEFI  Secure Boot on                 rescue 
 ┌ Steps ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ 
 │  > 1 Language    [ ] 2 Hardware check   [ ] 3 Disks   [ ] 4 Network   [ ] 5│ 
 └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ 
 ┌ Rescue a broken install ───────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ 
 │                                                                            │ 
 │ The installer looks for Crustates on this machine's disks. It reads them   │ 
 │ and changes nothing until you choose a repair.                             │ 
 │                                                                            │ 
 │ Found                                                                      │ 
 │   /dev/nvme0n1p3: 0.2.0 (4f2a9c01d3e5), boots next · 0.1.0 (9b1e77aa0c2d)  │ 
 │                                                                            │ 
 │ Repairs                                                                    │ 
 │   p  boot the previous OS image next                                       │ 
 │   n  reset the network to DHCP on every port                               │ 
 │   z  list the ZFS pools (they are not imported)                            │ 
 │   enter  reboot                                                            │ 
 │                                                                            │ 
 │ Repairing the boot loader comes in a later release.                        │ 
 │                                                                            │ 
 │                                                                            │ 
 │                                                                            │ 
